<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* Bootstrap 5.3.3, VENDORED AND TRACKED — the one file under wwwroot/lib that
       .gitignore re-includes (issue halheinrich/backgammon#126). Nothing in this
       repo restores wwwroot/lib: no libman.json, no npm step, no MSBuild target,
       so an ignored copy is a copy that exists on one machine, and CI and every
       fresh clone build the app unstyled. Committing the file is what makes a
       clone styled with no network at all; LibMan was rejected for the opposite
       reason (a restore step is one more thing that can be offline at build
       time). Upgrading means replacing the file AND this line together — the
       version lives here because this is the only place that names the file. An
       e2e pin (StylesheetTests) fails if the stylesheet stops being applied. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["BgQuiz_Blazor.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    @* Static fallback: the interactive outlet below cannot set a title until the
       ~19.5 MB WASM payload boots, and never does so for crawlers or no-JS clients. *@
    <title>BgQuiz</title>
    @* Every routable page is .Client-side with prerender: false, so a bare (static-pass)
       outlet would never receive their <PageTitle>. Emits nothing into the static pass,
       so there is no duplicate-<title> hazard. *@
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="@(new InteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    @* The navigation-fold applier, after blazor.web.js because it registers a
       Blazor.addEventListener('enhancedload') handler — and here in the host
       shell rather than anywhere in the .Client, because it must run on every
       page whether or not the WASM runtime has booted. Same @Assets helper as
       its sibling above: a stale cached applier after a deploy would fail
       silently. See wwwroot/js/navFold.js for the contract it holds with
       QuizSettings and MainLayout. *@
    <script src="@Assets["js/navFold.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
